# Level 2-05: Hold and Cross — combines a single ghost holding a single plate (the 1-04/4-02
# style "one ghost, one plate, one door" shape, not the full two-plate AND from 2-01) with a
# MovingPlatform crossing a one-tile gap just past that door. One-tile-wide spine at x=5, spawn
# (5,0), branch to plate a: (5,4)-(4,4)-(3,4)-(2,4)-(1,4), a dead end off the spine exactly like
# 2-01/2-04's branches. Door (gated by plate a alone) sits at (5,8). Past the door, platform
# waypoints P (5,9, order 0) and Q (5,11, order 1) straddle a solid one-tile chasm at (5,10) —
# same deliberate, hand-verified exception to "everything walkable back to spawn" that
# 2-03/4-03 use for their own platform gaps, since MovingPlatform jumps instantly between named
# coordinates with nothing to walk through in between. From Q it's a plain two-tile walk up to
# the goal at (5,13). Every tile is a single-width extension of the spine, connected back to
# spawn; nothing is enclosed by more than one connection.
#
# Loop 0 (record the ghost, alone):
#   t0-3 Up x4 to (5,4). t4-7 Left x4 to (1,4)=plate a, active end of t7. Loop runs its timer;
#   ghost1 spawns, holding a forever after.
# Loop 1 (final — ghost1 replays the script above; live player crosses the platform too):
#   Convoy (one already-moving actor -> player idles exactly 1 tick, then follows exactly one
#   tile behind, full derivation in 2-01/MoveResolver.cs):
#   t0 Ghost1 Up (5,0)->(5,1). Player idles.
#   t1 Ghost1 Up (5,1)->(5,2) [vacates (5,1)]. Player Up (5,0)->(5,1) [legal].
#   t2 Ghost1 Up (5,2)->(5,3) [vacates (5,2)]. Player Up (5,1)->(5,2) [legal].
#   t3 Ghost1 Up (5,3)->(5,4) [vacates (5,3)]. Player Up (5,2)->(5,3) [legal].
#   t4 Ghost1 Left (5,4)->(4,4) [vacates (5,4)]. Player Up (5,3)->(5,4) [legal — passes the
#     plate-a junction without turning]. Ghost1 continues down its own branch on ticks5-7,
#     unrelated to the player's path from here on, and idles on plate a forever after t7.
#   From here the player is alone on the spine.
#   t5 Up (5,4)->(5,5). t6 Up (5,5)->(5,6). t7 Up (5,6)->(5,7).
#   t8 Up: target (5,8)=door. Plate a activated at the end of (this loop's) t7 — same tick
#     index as loop 0, since ghost1's replay is byte-identical — so the door has been open
#     since the start of t8; the move succeeds with no bump: (5,7)->(5,8).
#   t9 Up (5,8)->(5,9)=P. WaypointAt(8)=WaypointAt(9)=P (floor(8/4)=floor(9/4)=2, even -> P
#     index), so the platform is simply sitting there when the player steps on; no surprise.
#   t10 Idle (still inside the P window: floor(10/4)=2 -> P).
#   t11 Idle (floor(11/4)=2 -> P still).
#   t12 Idle: the transition tick. WaypointAt(11)=P, WaypointAt(12)=floor(12/4)=3, odd -> Q.
#     The player, having idled through t10-t12, still has a post-move position of P at the end
#     of t12 — matching the platform's pre-tick position — so the carry rule relocates them
#     with it: (5,9)->(5,11).
#   t13 Up (5,11)->(5,12). t14 Up (5,12)->(5,13)=goal. WinCondition satisfied at tick 14.
# Totals: 2 loops used (1 ghost + 1 final) -> PAR_LOOPS: 2 (true minimum — this puzzle only
#   needs one of the two available timeline slots, same as 2-02; MAX_TIMELINES stays 2 per the
#   World 2 brief).
#   14 ticks in the winning loop -> PAR_TICKS: 19 (generous buffer).
NAME: 2-05 Hold and Cross
WORLD: 2
LOOP_SECONDS: 18
MAX_TIMELINES: 2
PAR_LOOPS: 2
PAR_TICKS: 19
GRID:
#####G#####
#####.#####
#####Q#####
###########
#####P#####
#####D#####
#####.#####
#####.#####
#####.#####
#1....#####
#####.#####
#####.#####
#####.#####
#####S#####
LEGEND:
S=spawn G=goal 1=plate:a D=door:and:a P=platform:plat2:0:4 Q=platform:plat2:1:4
